  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through next Friday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Thunderstorms are kicking off in \ncentral Nevada and are expected to spread into the eastern part of\nnorthern Nevada over the next several hours. Very warm conditions\nare also present, with heat advisories in effect in northern \nNevada through this evening. Above average temperatures are \nexpected to continue through the forecast period, with highs in \nthe 90s to very low triple digits, but the humidity is expected to\ndecrease over the next couple days. This is due to an upper level\nhigh pressure system over the plains shifting west and cutting \noff the monsoonal moisture flow. This will also decrease storm \nchances tomorrow and end them entirely starting Sunday. The high \nand associated ridging are favored to stay in place through the \nrest of the forecast, which would keep conditions dry and warm.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in thunderstorms\ntoday and tomorrow, although confidence is moderate regarding\nareal coverage tomorrow. High confidence in above average\ntemperatures over the next several days. Moderate confidence in\nthe forecast past Tuesday due to model variability regarding the\nupper air pattern. No changes were made to NBM output.",
